Job Description - Data Analyst Placement 2026-27 (341206)
 
Data Analyst Placement 2026-27
(Job Number: 341206)
 

About Us

Textron Specialized Vehicles is a leading global manufacturer of golf cars, utility and personal transportation vehicles, side-by-sides, all-terrain vehicles, professional turf-care equipment, and ground support equipment. 

At Ransomes Jacobsen Ltd., we design and manufacture professional turf-care equipment under the brands of Ransomes and Jacobsen. Our mission is to be the premier supplier of high-quality and environmentally conscious turf equipment, providing superior performance for our customers. From prestigious championship golf courses to the World Cup, for more than a century, the most important turf in the world has been manicured by our brand.

Opportunity

Ransomes Jacobsen Ltd (part of Textron Specialized Vehicles) are seeking a Data Analyst placement student, who will work within the Customer Care department, reporting to our Warranty Manager. As one of the world's leading manufacturers of commercial mowers and turf maintenance equipment, warranty is a key part of the service and customer care we provide our client's with. This 12-month internship is one of constant demand and changing priorities. We are looking for a student to start in the summer, who is willing to embrace responsibility within the warranty team. The successful candidate will analyse warranty data and liaise with external stakeholders on behalf of the Company.

Responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

Processing receipt of returns parts and coordinating transport to supplier;
Report progress of return item including internal performance & supplier recovery;
Managing internal & external enquiries, via email & telephone, ensuring excellent levels of customer service are delivered;
Supporting the reporting & analysis of the Warranty department Key Performance Indicator's (KPI);
Supporting the running of reports to enable data analysis & daily team functions;
Liaising with external stakeholders on behalf of the business, including dealers, suppliers, employees, and the senior management team;
Using data analytics as the basis for business change;
Auditing dealers (local and abroad) warranty processes and procedures;
Other duties as required.
 

Qualifications/Skills/Experience Required:

You should be enrolled in a Business/Finance/IT degree or similar subject that offers you the opportunity to take a placement year;

IT literate with Microsoft Office Applications;

Confident individual with a strong academic background;

Ability to analyse data and work on own initiative;

Self-motivated, with good communication and time-management skills;

Excellent attention to detail.

 

What we Offer:

Competitive salary;
A nine day working fortnight (every other Friday off work);
30 days holiday inclusive of Bank Holidays;
Company pension scheme (6% employer contribution);
Life assurance scheme;
Company sick pay scheme;
On-site golf course and football pitch;
Employee Assistance Programme;
Long service awards;
Perks at work (discounted cinema tickets etc);
Learning and development opportunities.
 
 
 
 
Recruiting Company Textron Specialized Vehicles
Primary Location Great Britain-England-Ipswich
Job Field Product Support
Schedule Full-time
Job Level Individual Contributor
Job Type Internship / Co-Op
Shift First Shift
Job Posting 04/16/2026, 9:06:47 AM

Job Description - Design Engineer Graduate (340811)
 
Design Engineer Graduate
(Job Number: 340811)
 

About Us

Textron Specialized Vehicles are a global manufacturer of golf cars, utility and personal transportation vehicles, side-by-sides, all-terrain vehicles, professional turf-care equipment, and ground support equipment.

At Ransomes Jacobsen Ltd, we design and manufacture professional turf-care equipment under the brands of Ransomes and Jacobsen. Our mission is to be the premier supplier of high-quality and environmentally conscious turf equipment, providing superior performance for our customers. From prestigious championship golf courses to the World Cup, for more than a century, the most important turf in the world has been manicured by our brand.

About the Role

This is a full-time role based at our manufacturing facility in Ipswich, Suffolk.

As a Design Engineer I, you will support the delivery of high-quality mechanical design work across a range of projects. Working under the guidance of senior-engineering staff, you will contribute to the development of reliable, cost-effective, and manufacturable solutions that meet performance targets and regulatory requirements.

Your responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

Produce mechanical designs that meet defined technical, performance, reliability, and cost requirements;
Create and maintain accurate engineering documentation, including drawings, Bills of Materials (BOMs), assembly instructions, and supporting technical publications in line with the Engineering Change process;
Apply best-practice design principles and utilise in-house standards, approved reference materials, and standard components wherever appropriate;
Ensure all designs are practical, efficient, and cost-effective to manufacture by working closely with Manufacturing and Production teams;
Ensure designs are developed in context, maintaining compatibility with adjacent components, assemblies, and wider system architectures;
Perform component-level CAE/FEA analyses to support design decisions, verify performance, and identify opportunities for improvement;
Integrate mistake-proofing, clear visual guidance, or simplified features into designs to reduce the potential for assembly errors or rework;
Collaborate with other Engineers and internal departments when implementing new design concepts or engineering approaches;
Interpret and incorporate relevant industry standards, directives, and regulatory requirements into product designs;
Support the engineering team in ensuring all documentation and designs comply with applicable quality and safety expectations;
Assist in the development of test plans and validation activities to ensure key design elements and performance objectives are met;
Support testing activities as required, including preparing test articles, reviewing results, and contributing to design refinements.
 

About You

As a Design Engineer I, we would ask you bring the following skills and experience:

Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in an Engineering discipline, ideally Mechanical Engineering.
Experience designing with a range of materials, including steels, plastics and alloys.
Exposure to engineering development processes such as prototyping, testing, or design-for-manufacture desirable.
Knowledge of DFME and PFMEA.
Proficiency in CAD software (NX preferred) required.
Familiarity with FEA tools, ideally ANSYS, to support basic analysis and validation activities.
Hands-on approach, with the ability to work effectively within a multidisciplinary team to take design concepts through to medium-volume production.
Self-motivated, capable of working independently toward defined objectives with minimal supervision.
Strong attention to detail, with proven problem-solving skills and a methodical approach to engineering tasks.
An interest in expanding knowledge across wider mechanical engineering disciplines as part of professional development.

Why us?

Work life balance promoted with every other Friday off;
30 days annual leave;
Competitive rate of pay, reviewed annually;
Enhanced Company pension;
Life assurance of four times your annual salary;
Comprehensive Employee Assistance Program for you and your immediate family;
Access to Textron University’s self-service training platform;
Eye care scheme;
Discounts on gym memberships, shopping and travel through Perks at Work;
Onsite golf course and football pitch;
Winter flu vaccination voucher.
 
 
 
 
Recruiting Company Textron Specialized Vehicles
Primary Location Great Britain-England-Ipswich
Job Field Engineering
Schedule Full-time
Job Level Individual Contributor
Job Type Standard
Shift First Shift
Job Posting 03/31/2026, 1:09:04 PM

Job Description - Quality Health Safety Environmental Engineer (340479)
 
Quality Health Safety Environmental Engineer
(Job Number: 340479)
 

About Us

Textron Specialized Vehicles are a global manufacturer of golf cars, utility and personal transportation vehicles, side-by-sides, all-terrain vehicles, professional turf-care equipment, and ground support equipment.

At Textron Sweden AB, we manufacture one-person–operated deicers under the Safeaero brand. We are committed to continuous innovation through rigorous research and development, as well as close collaboration with our customers to ensure our products meet their needs for safer, faster, and more cost‑efficient deicing operations. All Safeaero products are produced in Trelleborg, Sweden, and distributed to airlines and ground support service providers at some of the busiest and most deicing‑intensive airports worldwide.

About the Role

This is a full‑time position based at our manufacturing facility in Trelleborg, Sweden.

As a QHSE Engineer, you will support operations in ensuring that all quality, regulatory, and customer requirements are fully understood and met. You will also contribute to problem‑solving and continuous improvement activities across all departments, as well as manage tasks related to Environmental, Health, and Safety (EHS). Your responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

Leading and maintaining the ISO 9001 Quality Management System, ensuring compliance and driving continuous improvement of quality processes across the business;

Developing, implementing, and sustaining Quality Plans to support ongoing improvement of quality processes;

Implementing and monitoring KPIs for quality processes and recommending actions when performance does not meet required standards;

Ensuring that products and processes meet customer requirements and specifications;

Managing Environmental, Health and Safety (EHS) activities for the site, including:

Investigating product quality issues to:

protect the customer,

identify and implement immediate corrective actions to enable production at acceptable quality levels through root cause analysis, and

ensure long-term actions are implemented to prevent recurrence;

Managing Environmental, Health, and Safety (EHS) activities for the site, including:

Championing and monitoring health, safety, and environmental practices to ensure compliance with all relevant laws and regulations;

Supporting and advising the business on all aspects of health, safety, and environmental matters and best practice;

Organising and delivering EHS training to employees where appropriate;

Creating and maintaining a positive, proactive health and safety culture;

Providing guidance and promoting health, safety, and environmental awareness and compliance at all levels of the organisation;

Leading regular safety tours and making recommendations where necessary;

Performing other reasonable duties as required.

 

Educated, preferably to degree level, in a technical discipline;

Proven relevant experience within a Quality function;

Continuous improvement skills, e.g., LEAN methodologies;

Previous experience in managing Health and Safety matters;

Good working knowledge of ISO 9001 implementation or an equivalent standard;

Proficient in Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint);

Experience using SAP is advantageous;

Ability to present data accurately and effectively;

Strong analytical and interpersonal skills with a proactive mindset;

Ability to prioritise and manage conflicting demands while meeting operational deadlines;

Ability to influence and mentor colleagues to ensure ongoing compliance with Quality Management Systems;

Excellent problem solving and communication skills. 

 
 
 
 
